            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Error_500"
          }
        },
        "operationId": "get-api-system-ipx",
        "description": " # IPX object description\nIPX object is composed of 8 outputs relays, 8 digital inputs and 4 analog inputs. You can pilot external devices or measure external sensors values.\n\n### Object internal configuration:\n* **_id**: Unique ID of object \n* **errorCode**: Error code according to object auto check: dependencies, configuration values, etc. (0 if OK) \n\n### Object dependencies:\n* **ioDInput**: Array of 8 states representing each digital input. (\"on\" or \"off\")\n* **ioRelays**: Set \"on\", \"off\" or \"toggle\" to control each relay output.\n* **ioRelayState**: Array of 8 states representing each relays output. (\"on\" or \"off\")\n* **ana_IPX_Input**: Array of 8 values representing each analog input.\n* **ioCollInput**: Array of 8 states representing each opto isolate input. (\"on\" or \"off\")\n* **ioCollOutput**: Set \"on\", \"off\" or \"toggle\" to control each open collector output.\n* **ioCollOutputState**: Array of 8 states representing each open collector output. (\"on\" or \"off\")\n* **ioIPXReset**: Set \"on\" or \"toggle\" to reset IPX.\n* **ioDetectionAC**: Value representing ac detection in XPSU (\"on\" or \"off\")\n",
        "tags": [
          "ipx"
        ],
        "security": [
          {
            "ApiKey-Level_0": []
          }
        ]
      },
